                    If you want to start selling globally on platforms like Amazon, Shopify, or eBay, your local Pakistani business details might hold you back due to payment gateway restrictions. The ultimate solution is to <strong>form UK Ltd company from Pakistan for e-commerce</strong>. 
                </p>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4">Why Form a UK Ltd Company from Pakistan for E-commerce?</h3>
                <p>
                    Entrepreneurs in Pakistan often face hurdles when trying to access international payment gateways like Stripe, PayPal, or Shopify Payments. By opting to form a UK Ltd company from Pakistan for e-commerce, you unlock a world of opportunities:
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 mb-8">
                    <li><strong>Global Payment Gateways:</strong> Seamlessly integrate Stripe, PayPal, and Shopify Payments.</li>
                    <li><strong>Amazon FBA Ready:</strong> Easily set up Amazon Seller Central UK and expand across European marketplaces.</li>
                    <li><strong>Prestigious Business Address:</strong> Gain a London registered office address to build trust with international suppliers and customers.</li>
                    <li><strong>Business Banking:</strong> Open digital bank accounts like Wise or Tide in GBP, USD, and EUR, and withdraw funds directly to your Pakistani bank account.</li>
                    <li><strong>Limited Liability:</strong> Protect your personal assets from business liabilities.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4">Step-by-Step: How to Form UK Ltd Company from Pakistan for E-commerce</h3>
                
                <div class="space-y-8 mt-8">
                    <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100">
                        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-blue mb-2">Step 1: Choose a Unique Company Name</h4>
                        <p>The first step to form a UK Ltd company from Pakistan for e-commerce is selecting a name that is not already registered with UK Companies House. The name must end in "Ltd" or "Limited". Ensure it reflects your e-commerce brand.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100">
                        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-blue mb-2">Step 2: Select the Correct E-commerce SIC Code</h4>
                        <p>Standard Industrial Classification (SIC) codes tell Companies House what your business does. For e-commerce, the standard code is <strong>47910 (Retail sale via mail order houses or via Internet)</strong>. Getting this right is crucial for opening your business bank accounts later.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100">
                        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-blue mb-2">Step 3: Provide a UK Registered Address</h4>
                        <p>Every UK company needs a physical UK address. You don't need to rent an office. When you form a UK Ltd company from Pakistan for e-commerce using our services, we provide a prestigious London registered office address, keeping your home address in Pakistan private.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100">
                        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-blue mb-2">Step 4: Director and Shareholder Details</h4>
                        <p>You can be the sole director and 100% shareholder of your UK company. You only need your Pakistani passport and proof of address (like a utility bill or bank statement) for identity verification. No UK residency is required.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100">
                        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-blue mb-2">Step 5: Digital Submission & Approval</h4>
                        <p>We handle all the ACSP (Authorised Corporate Service Provider) identity verification required by the 2024 ECCTA regulations. We submit your application digitally, and companies are typically approved within 24 to 48 hours.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-4">Setting Up Payments: Wise, Stripe & Payoneer</h3>
                <p>
                    After you successfully form a UK Ltd company from Pakistan for e-commerce, the next hurdle is banking. With your UK company documents (Certificate of Incorporation, Memorandum & Articles of Association), you can apply for a <strong>Wise Business Account</strong> or <strong>Payoneer</strong>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    These accounts provide you with UK sort codes and account numbers. You can connect these bank accounts to Stripe or Shopify Payments. When you receive payments from international customers in GBP or USD, you can withdraw them directly to your local Pakistani bank account (like HBL, Meezan, or UBL) at excellent exchange rates.
                </p>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-4">Taxation: What Pakistani Founders Need to Know</h3>
                <p>
                    When you form a UK Ltd company from Pakistan for e-commerce, you must comply with UK tax laws. Your UK company pays Corporation Tax on profits generated. However, as a non-resident director living in Pakistan, you do not pay UK personal income tax on dividends if you do not live in the UK (though you must report income in Pakistan according to FBR rules).
                </p>
                <p>
                    Additionally, you only need to register for UK VAT if your taxable turnover exceeds £90,000 in a rolling 12-month period, or if you hold inventory in the UK (like Amazon FBA UK). Always consult with a UK accountant to ensure full compliance.
                </p>
            </div>
